Dashboard ecom_cohort_dashboard {
  title: 'Ecommerce Cohort Analysis'
  description: 'One tab per cohort use case. Each tab shows the same report built two ways — with the category filter applied during cohort profiling, and applied to final results — and carries its own independent filters.'
  owner: 'chukwudi@holistics.io'

  block txt_ret: TextBlock {
    content: @md ## Retention — two ways to apply the same filter

Both reports use the same dataset, metric and layout. **Category** and **Product** feed *both* — but land in a different place in each.

**Above:** the filter chooses who is in the cohort, before any metric runs, so each customer's whole history still counts. **Below:** the cohort forms first, then rows are trimmed on the way out.;;
  }

  block f_ret_month: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Cohort Month'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_users.cohort_month)
    }
    default {
      operator: 'matches'
      value: 'last 12 months'
    }
  }

  block f_ret_window: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Lifecycle Window (Month Number)'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_orders.month_number)
    }
    default {
      operator: 'between'
      value: [
        0,
        12
      ]
    }
  }

  block f_ret_country: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Country'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecommerce_countries.name)
    }
  }

  block f_ret_units: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Units Band at Acquisition'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_users.first_order_units_band)
    }
  }

  block f_ret_category: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Category'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecom_cohort_first_order_categories.parent_category)
    }
    settings {
      input_type: 'multiple'
    }
  }

  block f_ret_product: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Product'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      field: r(ecom_cohort_first_order_categories.product_name)
    }
    settings {
      input_type: 'multiple'
    }
  }

  block rep_ret_right: VizBlock {
    label: 'Retention — filter applied during cohort profiling'
    viz: PivotTable {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      rows: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Cohort'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_users.cohort_month)
          format {
            type: 'date'
            pattern: 'LLL yyyy'
          }
          uname: 'retr_row'
        }
      ]
      columns: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Month'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_orders.month_number)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,###0'
          }
          uname: 'retr_col'
        }
      ]
      values: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Retention'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis.cohort_retention)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,##0.0%'
          }
          uname: 'retr_val'
        }
      ]
      settings {
        conditional_formats: [
          ConditionalFormat {
            key: 'retr_val'
            format: ScaleFormat {
              min {
                value: 0
                color: '#FFFFFF'
              }
              mid {
                value: 0.5
                color: '#D1E5FA'
              }
              max {
                value: 1
                color: '#8DBEF2'
              }
            }
          }
        ]
        sorts: [
          SortSetting {
            key: 'retr_row'
            direction: 'asc'
          },
          SortSetting {
            key: 'retr_col'
            direction: 'asc'
          }
        ]
        frozen_columns: 1
        wrap_header_text: false
        pagination_size: 13
      }
    }
  }

  block rep_ret_wrong: VizBlock {
    label: 'Retention — filter applied to final results'
    viz: PivotTable {
      dataset: ecom_cohort_analysis
      rows: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Cohort'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_users.cohort_month)
          format {
            type: 'date'
            pattern: 'LLL yyyy'
          }
          uname: 'retw_row'
        }
      ]
      columns: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Month'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis, ecommerce_orders.month_number)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,###0'
          }
          uname: 'retw_col'
        }
      ]
      values: [
        VizFieldFull {
          label: 'Retention'
          ref: r(ecom_cohort_analysis.cohort_retention)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,##0.0%'
          }
          uname: 'retw_val'
        }
      ]
      settings {
        conditional_formats: [
          ConditionalFormat {
            key: 'retw_val'
            format: ScaleFormat {
              min {
                value: 0
                color: '#FFFFFF'
              }
              mid {
                value: 0.5
                color: '#D1E5FA'
              }
              max {
                value: 1
                color: '#8DBEF2'
              }
            }
          }
        ]
        sorts: [
          SortSetting {
            key: 'retw_row'
            direction: 'asc'
          },
          SortSetting {
            key: 'retw_col'
            direction: 'asc'
          }
        ]
        frozen_columns: 1
        wrap_header_text: false
        pagination_size: 13
      }
    }
  }

  block txt_ret_why: TextBlock {
    content: @md **What the difference does.** Retention sags because only orders containing the chosen category count as activity, so a returning customer who bought something else reads as churned.

**The second report describes a different population.** Filtering at the final-results level selects everyone who *ever* bought the category rather than those who bought it at acquisition, so Cohort Size itself moves: for Jan 2026 / Skin Care it reads 210 against 83. Month 0 is where it shows plainest — every acquired customer orders in their acquisition month by definition, so retention there is 100% when the filter profiles the cohort, and 44.8% when it only trims the output.;;
  }

